infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Saturation, not utilization, predicts latency
  desc Same lesson, two disks: the busier one is healthier — what matters is the queue
  compares
    - label Disk A — looks calmer
      children
        - label Utilization 80%
          desc Busy four-fifths of the time — looks fine on a usage gauge
        - label Queue depth 50
          desc 50 jobs waiting; every one pays the full queueing delay
        - label Verdict — far worse
          desc Saturation is the leading indicator of user-visible latency
    - label Disk B — looks busier
      children
        - label Utilization 95%
          desc Nearly pinned — would alarm a utilization-only dashboard
        - label Queue depth 1
          desc Almost nothing waiting; it is just keeping pace
        - label Verdict — fine
          desc 100% utilization is healthy when no work is queued behind it
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
